Implement user story SKY-004-impl: Implement Express REST API server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts — an Express HTTP server exposing /health, /search, /cheapest, and a static dashboard at /. Server reads PORT (default 3000) and RAPIDAPI_KEY from env; API routes return 503 if key absent. Also create src/public/index.html dashboard and configure build scripts. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Express server (src/server.ts) exports named `app` and guards `listen()` so test imports never bind a port
- GET /health returns 200 JSON {status:'ok',uptime:<number>} regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- GET /search validates required params (from,to,date), defaults adults to 1, rejects non-numeric adults, and returns {flights,count,searchedAt}
- GET /cheapest validates required params, returns single cheapest FlightResult or 404, forwards adults param
- GET / serves src/public/index.html read from file at runtime (not hardcoded inline HTML)
- RAPIDAPI_KEY absence gates /search and /cheapest (503) but not /health or /
- SkyscannerClient errors produce 500 JSON without crashing; searchedAt is distinct ISO-8601 per request; FlightResult imported from SKY-002
- src/public/index.html is a styled dashboard with header, search form, results area, and client-side JS
- package.json has 'start' and 'build' scripts; build copies src/public/ to dist/public/





